@startuml
title Loommux Pueue Execution 生命周期
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam state {
  BackgroundColor white
}

[*] --> Queued : accepted
Queued --> Stashed : external stash
Stashed --> Queued : external / scheduled enqueue
Queued --> Locked : edit
Stashed --> Locked : edit
Locked --> Queued : restore
Locked --> Stashed : restore
Queued --> Running : daemon starts task
Stashed --> Running : external force-start
Running --> Paused : external pause
Paused --> Running : external resume
Queued --> Failed : spawn / dependency failure
Stashed --> Failed : force-start spawn failure
Running --> Completed : Success
Running --> Failed : Failed / Errored
Running --> Killed : Done(Killed)
Paused --> Completed : Success
Paused --> Failed : Failed / Errored
Paused --> Killed : Done(Killed)
Queued --> Cancelled : Remove control succeeds
Stashed --> Cancelled : Remove control succeeds

Completed --> [*]
Failed --> [*]
Killed --> [*]
Cancelled --> [*]

note right of Locked
  Locked is a backend edit overlay.
  Loommux only observes it;
  cancel returns cancel_blocked.
  Other state writes are unsupported.
  Identity is validated after restore.
end note

note bottom of Cancelled
  Cancelled proves Remove success.
  A racing backend result may be unobserved;
  frozen output remains incomplete.
  All public terminal records are frozen.
  External in-place restart is unsupported
  and never reopens an execution.
end note
@enduml
